      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: When `CONFIG_CHARGER` is disabled, if the host sets `p-\u003emode` to a valid non-normal mode like `CHARGE_CONTROL_IDLE`, this code will silently accept it and return `EC_HOST_CMD_SUCCESS`. However, because the mode is not persisted in BBRAM and there is no `local_state` to store it in memory, a subsequent `GET` command will return `CHARGE_CONTROL_NORMAL`. We should probably reject non-normal modes with `EC_HOST_CMD_INVALID_PARAM` or `EC_HOST_CMD_UNAVAILABLE` if `CONFIG_CHARGER` is disabled, since the EC cannot enforce or even remember them.",
